==== HOW TO READ IT ====
  For each (cores, N) cell compute s = (T(L) - T(1)) / (L - 1) at L = 8 and 16.
  Then compare s ACROSS N at fixed cores:
    s roughly doubles when N doubles -> the B re-read is real and HBM-priced.
    s barely moves when N doubles    -> it is a fixed per-iteration cost; do NOT
                                        add re-read bytes, add a per-iteration term.
    s grows sub-linearly             -> partial residency; report s / (B/BW) as the
                                        measured HBM fraction of each re-read.
  Compare s ACROSS cores at fixed N to attribute any residual to per-tile underfill.
  Fold with: python3 notes/parse_sweep_logs.py, then re-run
  python3 notes/test_loop_invariant_reread.py to re-score with real B variation.
